    l1: share one settled F6 run among the tests that only read it

    Four F6 tests (off-origin, allowlisted CDN, font hosts, runtime
    widening) each launched the app identically, waited for the same
    settle, then only read the harness instruments. Take that run once,
    snapshot the page report, the fake's counters and the proxy journal,
    and let each test assert its own claim on the snapshot. A run is cached
    only if it settled; a test run alone takes its own launch.

    Strict mode reads its post-toggle state through the same snapshot type.
    Saves three launches and page settles, ~38 s of L1.

